# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/prefix-tiers development window (the preconverted GDN checkpoints and the host KV tier; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/prefix-tiers and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are
# resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-prefix-tiers-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/prefix-tiers head (sed -i 's/tp4-prefix-tiers-1/<tag>/' *.env); every later job serves that one
# image. A commit of a file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# X0 (STOP): the cards' status, the rescan (the first quad job after a hardware change or a long idle), and a reset. READ: the status prints, the rescan finds every board, the reset completes on all four.
# No other window driver may be alive. Duration (estimate): 20 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status rescan reset
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-prefix-tiers-1
